---
import { pageDates } from "../page-dates.js";
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import { SITE, AUTHOR } from "../site.config.js";
---
<PageLayout
  title={`About ${SITE.name}`}
  description={`${SITE.name} offers free SAT practice by skill and free English tests, including TOEFL-style practice, with an explanation for every answer choice.`}
  updated={pageDates("/about/").updated ?? pageDates("/about/").published}
>
  <p>{SITE.name} is a free place to practice the SAT one skill at a time, and to test your English level, vocabulary and grammar. Every question comes with an explanation of the right answer and of each wrong one.</p>
  <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
  <p>Most free SAT practice either runs out quickly or explains only the right answer. We wanted unlimited practice on the skills where students lose the most points, with explanations that name the exact mistake behind each wrong choice.</p>
  <h2>What you'll find here</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/sat/math/">SAT Math practice</a> across all four domains, with new questions every set.</li>
    <li><a href="/sat/reading-writing/">SAT Reading and Writing practice</a> for punctuation, grammar, transitions, vocabulary in context and more.</li>
    <li><a href="/sat/">A guide to the digital SAT's format</a> and <a href="/guides/">strategy guides</a>.</li>
    <li><a href="/english/">English tests</a>: a level test from A1 to C2, a vocabulary test, a grammar test and short tests on pronouns and verb tenses.</li>
    <li><a href="/toefl/">TOEFL reading and writing practice</a>, with the current TOEFL iBT format as ETS publishes it.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Who runs it</h2>
  <p>{SITE.name} is built and written by <a href={`/author/${AUTHOR.slug}/`}>{AUTHOR.name}</a>, a computer engineer. It is independent and not affiliated with College Board. SAT® is a trademark registered by the College Board, which is not affiliated with, and does not endorse, this site.</p>
  <h2>How it's funded</h2>
  <p>Practice is free and needs no account. The site may show advertising to cover hosting; advertisers have no influence over what we publish. See the <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.</p>
  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>Found a mistake in a question? Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
